What you are after is a Spatially Varying Coefficient (SVC) model. These can be analyzed in INLA using both aerial data and models (CAR) and continuous data and models (SPDE). Essentially, this is a random slope model where the random slope parameter is modeled with spatial structure. Looks like you want to do it using SPDE. The only tricky part is setting up the data stacks. Maybe you can do a bit of reading on SVC models and then I can help you code it in INLA?

