Hello,

I am currently working on a regression model including a random slope with a spatiotemporal interaction term. Since I wanted to compare results from four different types of spatiotemporal interaction, I tried

form.m42c <- y ~
  f(GEOID, model = "bym", graph = graph, constr = TRUE, hyper = hyp.prior) +
  f(year1, model = 'ar1', constr = TRUE) + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8

form.t42III <- update(form.m42c, ~ . + f(year3, x1, model = "iid", group = GEOID2,
                                         control.group = list(graph = graph, model = 'besag'),
                                      constr = TRUE) )

finla <- inla(formula = form.t42III, data = data.pu,
              control.compute = list(waic = TRUE, dic = TRUE, cpo = TRUE,
                                       openmp.strategy = 'large'),
              verbose = TRUE,
              control.inla = control.inla(cmin = -0.0, h=0.77, b.strategy = 'keep', strategy = "simplified.laplace",
                                            int.strategy = "eb", restart = 3, optimiser = 'gsl',
                                            stupid.search.factor = 1.25), #diagonal = 1e4
              control.fixed = list(prec.intercept = 0.0001),
              control.predictor = list(compute = TRUE),
              control.mode = list(restart = FALSE, fixed = FALSE))

However, the model consumed all of my memory then crashed. I think my machine has a decent amount of RAM (64GB, FYI), and there was no problem with fitting models with type-I, II, and IV spatiotemporal interaction term.

Could you explain why the model with the type-III spatiotemporal interaction term is only crashed?

Thank you very much.

