You can try to reduce the number of threads, which will reduce the
amount of memory (option num.threads)

also control.inla=list(strategy="adaptive")

would help.

It looks like you value for h=0.77 is very high, and the default value
as of now, is 0.005.

You may also want to try the new testing version of today which is
faster (then remove restart, optimiser), and you may want to check out
the PARDISO library, see

inla.pardiso()

